{"route":"/docs/5.0/utilities/api/","version":"5.0","renderedVersion":"5.0","title":{"id":"content","type":"heading","en":"Utility API","level":1},"lead":{"id":"content--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"The utility API is a Sass-based tool to generate utility classes."},"blocks":[{"id":"content--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"Bootstrap utilities are generated with our utility API and can be used to modify or extend our default set of utility classes via Sass. Our utility API is based on a series of Sass maps and functions for generating families of classes with various options. If you’re unfamiliar with Sass maps, read up on the <a href=\"https://sass-lang.com/documentation/values/maps\">official Sass docs</a> to get started."},{"id":"content--paragraph-3","type":"paragraph","en":"The <code>$utilities</code> map contains all our utilities and is later merged with your custom <code>$utilities</code> map, if present. The utility map contains a keyed list of utility groups which accept the following options:"},{"id":"content--table-1","type":"table","caption":[],"rows":[{"head":true,"cells":[{"type":"th","body":[{"id":"content--paragraph-4","type":"paragraph","en":"Option"}]},{"type":"th","body":[{"id":"content--paragraph-5","type":"paragraph","en":"Type"}]},{"type":"th","body":[{"id":"content--paragraph-6","type":"paragraph","en":"Description"}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"content--paragraph-7","type":"paragraph","en":"<code>property</code>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"content--paragraph-8","type":"paragraph","en":"<strong>Required</strong>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"content--paragraph-9","type":"paragraph","en":"Name of the property, this can be a string or an array of strings (e.g., horizontal paddings or margins)."}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"content--paragraph-10","type":"paragraph","en":"<code>values</code>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"content--paragraph-11","type":"paragraph","en":"<strong>Required</strong>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"content--paragraph-12","type":"paragraph","en":"List of values, or a map if you don’t want the class name to be the same as the value. If <code>null</code> is used as map key, it isn’t compiled."}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"content--paragraph-13","type":"paragraph","en":"<code>class</code>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"content--paragraph-14","type":"paragraph","en":"Optional"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"content--paragraph-15","type":"paragraph","en":"Variable for the class name if you don’t want it to be the same as the property. In case you don’t provide the <code>class</code> key and <code>property</code> key is an array of strings, the class name will be the first element of the <code>property</code> array."}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"content--paragraph-16","type":"paragraph","en":"<code>state</code>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"content--paragraph-17","type":"paragraph","en":"Optional"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"content--paragraph-18","type":"paragraph","en":"List of pseudo-class variants like <code>:hover</code> or <code>:focus</code> to generate for the utility. No default value."}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"content--paragraph-19","type":"paragraph","en":"<code>responsive</code>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"content--paragraph-20","type":"paragraph","en":"Optional"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"content--paragraph-21","type":"paragraph","en":"Boolean indicating if responsive classes need to be generated. <code>false</code> by default."}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"content--paragraph-22","type":"paragraph","en":"<code>rfs</code>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"content--paragraph-23","type":"paragraph","en":"Optional"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"content--paragraph-24","type":"paragraph","en":"Boolean to enable fluid rescaling. Have a look at the <a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.0/getting-started/rfs/\">RFS</a> page to find out how this works. <code>false</code> by default."}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"content--paragraph-25","type":"paragraph","en":"<code>print</code>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"content--paragraph-26","type":"paragraph","en":"Optional"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"content--paragraph-27","type":"paragraph","en":"Boolean indicating if print classes need to be generated. <code>false</code> by default."}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"content--paragraph-28","type":"paragraph","en":"<code>rtl</code>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"content--paragraph-29","type":"paragraph","en":"Optional"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"content--paragraph-30","type":"paragraph","en":"Boolean indicating if utility should be kept in RTL. <code>true</code> by default."}]}]}]},{"id":"api-explained","type":"heading","en":"API explained","level":2},{"id":"api-explained--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"All utility variables are added to the <code>$utilities</code> variable within our <code>_utilities.scss</code> stylesheet. Each group of utilities looks something like this:"},{"id":"api-explained--code-1","type":"code","value":"$utilities: (\n  \"opacity\": (\n    property: opacity,\n    values: (\n      0: 0,\n      25: .25,\n      50: .5,\n      75: .75,\n      100: 1,\n    )\n  )\n );","language":"scss"},{"id":"api-explained--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"Which outputs the following:"},{"id":"api-explained--code-2","type":"code","value":".opacity-0 { opacity: 0; }\n.opacity-25 { opacity: .25; }\n.opacity-50 { opacity: .5; }\n.opacity-75 { opacity: .75; }\n.opacity-100 { opacity: 1; }","language":"css"},{"id":"custom-class-prefix","type":"heading","en":"Custom class prefix","level":3},{"id":"custom-class-prefix--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Use the <code>class</code> option to change the class prefix used in the compiled CSS:"},{"id":"custom-class-prefix--code-1","type":"code","value":"$utilities: (\n  \"opacity\": (\n    property: opacity,\n    class: o,\n    values: (\n      0: 0,\n      25: .25,\n      50: .5,\n      75: .75,\n      100: 1,\n    )\n  )\n );","language":"scss"},{"id":"custom-class-prefix--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"Output:"},{"id":"custom-class-prefix--code-2","type":"code","value":".o-0 { opacity: 0; }\n.o-25 { opacity: .25; }\n.o-50 { opacity: .5; }\n.o-75 { opacity: .75; }\n.o-100 { opacity: 1; }","language":"css"},{"id":"states","type":"heading","en":"States","level":3},{"id":"states--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Use the <code>state</code> option to generate pseudo-class variations. Example pseudo-classes are <code>:hover</code> and <code>:focus</code>. When a list of states are provided, classnames are created for that pseudo-class. For example, to change opacity on hover, add <code>state: hover</code> and you’ll get <code>.opacity-hover:hover</code> in your compiled CSS."},{"id":"states--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"Need multiple pseudo-classes? Use a space-separated list of states: <code>state: hover focus</code>."},{"id":"states--code-1","type":"code","value":"$utilities: (\n  \"opacity\": (\n    property: opacity,\n    class: opacity,\n    state: hover,\n    values: (\n      0: 0,\n      25: .25,\n      50: .5,\n      75: .75,\n      100: 1,\n    )\n  )\n);","language":"scss"},{"id":"states--paragraph-3","type":"paragraph","en":"Output:"},{"id":"states--code-2","type":"code","value":".opacity-0-hover:hover { opacity: 0 !important; }\n.opacity-25-hover:hover { opacity: .25 !important; }\n.opacity-50-hover:hover { opacity: .5 !important; }\n.opacity-75-hover:hover { opacity: .75 !important; }\n.opacity-100-hover:hover { opacity: 1 !important; }","language":"css"},{"id":"responsive-utilities","type":"heading","en":"Responsive utilities","level":3},{"id":"responsive-utilities--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Add the <code>responsive</code> boolean to generate responsive utilities (e.g., <code>.opacity-md-25</code>) across <a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.0/layout/breakpoints/\">all breakpoints</a>."},{"id":"responsive-utilities--code-1","type":"code","value":"$utilities: (\n  \"opacity\": (\n    property: opacity,\n    responsive: true,\n    values: (\n      0: 0,\n      25: .25,\n      50: .5,\n      75: .75,\n      100: 1,\n    )\n  )\n );","language":"scss"},{"id":"responsive-utilities--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"Output:"},{"id":"responsive-utilities--code-2","type":"code","value":".opacity-0 { opacity: 0 !important; }\n.opacity-25 { opacity: .25 !important; }\n.opacity-50 { opacity: .5 !important; }\n.opacity-75 { opacity: .75 !important; }\n.opacity-100 { opacity: 1 !important; }\n\n@media (min-width: 576px) {\n  .opacity-sm-0 { opacity: 0 !important; }\n  .opacity-sm-25 { opacity: .25 !important; }\n  .opacity-sm-50 { opacity: .5 !important; }\n  .opacity-sm-75 { opacity: .75 !important; }\n  .opacity-sm-100 { opacity: 1 !important; }\n}\n\n@media (min-width: 768px) {\n  .opacity-md-0 { opacity: 0 !important; }\n  .opacity-md-25 { opacity: .25 !important; }\n  .opacity-md-50 { opacity: .5 !important; }\n  .opacity-md-75 { opacity: .75 !important; }\n  .opacity-md-100 { opacity: 1 !important; }\n}\n\n@media (min-width: 992px) {\n  .opacity-lg-0 { opacity: 0 !important; }\n  .opacity-lg-25 { opacity: .25 !important; }\n  .opacity-lg-50 { opacity: .5 !important; }\n  .opacity-lg-75 { opacity: .75 !important; }\n  .opacity-lg-100 { opacity: 1 !important; }\n}\n\n@media (min-width: 1200px) {\n  .opacity-xl-0 { opacity: 0 !important; }\n  .opacity-xl-25 { opacity: .25 !important; }\n  .opacity-xl-50 { opacity: .5 !important; }\n  .opacity-xl-75 { opacity: .75 !important; }\n  .opacity-xl-100 { opacity: 1 !important; }\n}\n\n@media (min-width: 1400px) {\n  .opacity-xxl-0 { opacity: 0 !important; }\n  .opacity-xxl-25 { opacity: .25 !important; }\n  .opacity-xxl-50 { opacity: .5 !important; }\n  .opacity-xxl-75 { opacity: .75 !important; }\n  .opacity-xxl-100 { opacity: 1 !important; }\n}","language":"css"},{"id":"changing-utilities","type":"heading","en":"Changing utilities","level":3},{"id":"changing-utilities--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Override existing utilities by using the same key. For example, if you want additional responsive overflow utility classes, you can do this:"},{"id":"changing-utilities--code-1","type":"code","value":"$utilities: (\n  \"overflow\": (\n    responsive: true,\n    property: overflow,\n    values: visible hidden scroll auto,\n  ),\n);","language":"scss"},{"id":"print-utilities","type":"heading","en":"Print utilities","level":3},{"id":"print-utilities--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Enabling the <code>print</code> option will <strong>also</strong> generate utility classes for print, which are only applied within the <code>@media print { ... }</code> media query."},{"id":"print-utilities--code-1","type":"code","value":"$utilities: (\n  \"opacity\": (\n    property: opacity,\n    print: true,\n    values: (\n      0: 0,\n      25: .25,\n      50: .5,\n      75: .75,\n      100: 1,\n    )\n  )\n );","language":"scss"},{"id":"print-utilities--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"Output:"},{"id":"print-utilities--code-2","type":"code","value":".opacity-0 { opacity: 0 !important; }\n.opacity-25 { opacity: .25 !important; }\n.opacity-50 { opacity: .5 !important; }\n.opacity-75 { opacity: .75 !important; }\n.opacity-100 { opacity: 1 !important; }\n\n@media print {\n  .opacity-print-0 { opacity: 0 !important; }\n  .opacity-print-25 { opacity: .25 !important; }\n  .opacity-print-50 { opacity: .5 !important; }\n  .opacity-print-75 { opacity: .75 !important; }\n  .opacity-print-100 { opacity: 1 !important; }\n}","language":"css"},{"id":"importance","type":"heading","en":"Importance","level":2},{"id":"importance--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"All utilities generated by the API include <code>!important</code> to ensure they override components and modifier classes as intended. You can toggle this setting globally with the <code>$enable-important-utilities</code> variable (defaults to <code>true</code>)."},{"id":"using-the-api","type":"heading","en":"Using the API","level":2},{"id":"using-the-api--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Now that you’re familiar with how the utilities API works, learn how to add your own custom classes and modify our default utilities."},{"id":"add-utilities","type":"heading","en":"Add utilities","level":3},{"id":"add-utilities--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"New utilities can be added to the default <code>$utilities</code> map with a <code>map-merge</code>. Make sure our required Sass files and <code>_utilities.scss</code> are imported first, then use the <code>map-merge</code> to add your additional utilities. For example, here’s how to add a responsive <code>cursor</code> utility with three values."},{"id":"add-utilities--code-1","type":"code","value":"@import \"bootstrap/scss/functions\";\n@import \"bootstrap/scss/variables\";\n@import \"bootstrap/scss/utilities\";\n\n$utilities: map-merge(\n  $utilities,\n  (\n    \"cursor\": (\n      property: cursor,\n      class: cursor,\n      responsive: true,\n      values: auto pointer grab,\n    )\n  )\n);","language":"scss"},{"id":"modify-utilities","type":"heading","en":"Modify utilities","level":3},{"id":"modify-utilities--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Modify existing utilities in the default <code>$utilities</code> map with <code>map-get</code> and <code>map-merge</code> functions. In the example below, we’re adding an additional value to the <code>width</code> utilities. Start with an initial <code>map-merge</code> and then specify which utility you want to modify. From there, fetch the nested <code>&quot;width&quot;</code> map with <code>map-get</code> to access and modify the utility’s options and values."},{"id":"modify-utilities--code-1","type":"code","value":"@import \"bootstrap/scss/functions\";\n@import \"bootstrap/scss/variables\";\n@import \"bootstrap/scss/utilities\";\n\n$utilities: map-merge(\n  $utilities,\n  (\n    \"width\": map-merge(\n      map-get($utilities, \"width\"),\n      (\n        values: map-merge(\n          map-get(map-get($utilities, \"width\"), \"values\"),\n          (10: 10%),\n        ),\n      ),\n    ),\n  )\n);","language":"scss"},{"id":"enable-responsive","type":"heading","en":"Enable responsive","level":4},{"id":"enable-responsive--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"You can enable responsive classes for an existing set of utilities that are not currently responsive by default. For example, to make the <code>border</code> classes responsive:"},{"id":"enable-responsive--code-1","type":"code","value":"@import \"bootstrap/scss/functions\";\n@import \"bootstrap/scss/variables\";\n@import \"bootstrap/scss/utilities\";\n\n$utilities: map-merge(\n  $utilities, (\n    \"border\": map-merge(\n      map-get($utilities, \"border\"),\n      ( responsive: true ),\n    ),\n  )\n);","language":"scss"},{"id":"enable-responsive--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"This will now generate responsive variations of <code>.border</code> and <code>.border-0</code> for each breakpoint. Your generated CSS will look like this:"},{"id":"enable-responsive--code-2","type":"code","value":".border { ... }\n.border-0 { ... }\n\n@media (min-width: 576px) {\n  .border-sm { ... }\n  .border-sm-0 { ... }\n}\n\n@media (min-width: 768px) {\n  .border-md { ... }\n  .border-md-0 { ... }\n}\n\n@media (min-width: 992px) {\n  .border-lg { ... }\n  .border-lg-0 { ... }\n}\n\n@media (min-width: 1200px) {\n  .border-xl { ... }\n  .border-xl-0 { ... }\n}\n\n@media (min-width: 1400px) {\n  .border-xxl { ... }\n  .border-xxl-0 { ... }\n}","language":"css"},{"id":"rename-utilities","type":"heading","en":"Rename utilities","level":4},{"id":"rename-utilities--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Missing v4 utilities, or used to another naming convention? The utilities API can be used to override the resulting <code>class</code> of a given utility—for example, to rename <code>.ms-*</code> utilities to oldish <code>.ml-*</code>:"},{"id":"rename-utilities--code-1","type":"code","value":"@import \"bootstrap/scss/functions\";\n@import \"bootstrap/scss/variables\";\n@import \"bootstrap/scss/utilities\";\n\n$utilities: map-merge(\n  $utilities, (\n    \"margin-start\": map-merge(\n      map-get($utilities, \"margin-start\"),\n      ( class: ml ),\n    ),\n  )\n);","language":"scss"},{"id":"remove-utilities","type":"heading","en":"Remove utilities","level":3},{"id":"remove-utilities--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Remove any of the default utilities by setting the group key to <code>null</code>. For example, to remove all our <code>width</code> utilities, create a <code>$utilities</code> <code>map-merge</code> and add <code>&quot;width&quot;: null</code> within."},{"id":"remove-utilities--code-1","type":"code","value":"@import \"bootstrap/scss/functions\";\n@import \"bootstrap/scss/variables\";\n@import \"bootstrap/scss/utilities\";\n\n$utilities: map-merge(\n  $utilities,\n  (\n    \"width\": null\n  )\n);","language":"scss"},{"id":"remove-utility-in-rtl","type":"heading","en":"Remove utility in RTL","level":4},{"id":"remove-utility-in-rtl--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Some edge cases make <a href=\"https://rtlstyling.com/posts/rtl-styling#common-things-that-might-not-work-for-rtl\">RTL styling difficult</a>, such as line breaks in Arabic. Thus utilities can be dropped from RTL output by setting the <code>rtl</code> option to <code>false</code>:"},{"id":"remove-utility-in-rtl--code-1","type":"code","value":"$utilities: (\n  \"word-wrap\": (\n    property: word-wrap word-break,\n    class: text,\n    values: (break: break-word),\n    rtl: false\n  ),\n);","language":"scss"},{"id":"remove-utility-in-rtl--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"Output:"},{"id":"remove-utility-in-rtl--code-2","type":"code","value":"/* rtl:begin:remove */\n.text-break {\n  word-wrap: break-word !important;\n  word-break: break-word !important;\n}\n/* rtl:end:remove */","language":"css"},{"id":"remove-utility-in-rtl--paragraph-3","type":"paragraph","en":"This doesn’t output anything in RTL, thanks to <a href=\"https://rtlcss.com/learn/usage-guide/control-directives/#remove\">the RTLCSS <code>remove</code> control directive</a>."}],"demos":[],"nav":[{"en":"Introduction","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.0/getting-started/introduction/"},{"en":"Download","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.0/getting-started/download/"},{"en":"Contents","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.0/getting-started/contents/"},{"en":"Browsers & devices","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.0/getting-started/browsers-devices/"},{"en":"JavaScript","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.0/getting-started/javascript/"},{"en":"Build tools","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.0/getting-started/build-tools/"},{"en":"Webpack","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.0/getting-started/webpack/"},{"en":"Parcel","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.0/getting-started/parcel/"},{"en":"Accessibility","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.0/getting-started/accessibility/"},{"en":"RFS","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.0/getting-started/rfs/"},{"en":"RTL","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.0/getting-started/rtl/"},{"en":"Overview","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.0/customize/overview/"},{"en":"Sass","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.0/customize/sass/"},{"en":"Options","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.0/customize/options/"},{"en":"Color","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.0/customize/color/"},{"en":"Components","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.0/customize/components/"},{"en":"CSS variables","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.0/customize/css-variables/"},{"en":"Optimize","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.0/customize/optimize/"},{"en":"Breakpoints","href":"https://getbootstr